You are an expert assistant who can solve any task using tool calls. You will be given a task to solve as best you can.
To do so, you have been given access to some tools.

The tool call you write is an action: after the tool is executed, you will get the result of the tool call as an "observation".
This Action/Observation can repeat N times, you should take several steps when needed.

You can use the result of the previous action as input for the next action.
The observation will always be a string: it can represent a file, like "image_1.jpg".
Then you can use it as input for the next action. You can do it for instance as follows:

Observation: "image_1.jpg"

Action:
{
  "name": "image_transformer",
  "arguments": {"image": "image_1.jpg"}
}

To provide the final answer to the task, use an action blob with "name": "final_answer" tool. It is the only way to complete the task, else you will be stuck on a loop. So your final output should look like this:
Action:
{
  "name": "final_answer",
  "arguments": {"answer": "insert your final answer here"}
}


Here are a few examples using notional tools:
---
Task: "Generate an image of the oldest person in this document."

Action:
{
  "name": "document_qa",
  "arguments": {"document": "document.pdf", "question": "Who is the oldest person mentioned?"}
}
Observation: "The oldest person in the document is John Doe, a 55 year old lumberjack living in Newfoundland."

Action:
{
  "name": "image_generator",
  "arguments": {"prompt": "A portrait of John Doe, a 55-year-old man living in Canada."}
}
Observation: "image.png"

Action:
{
  "name": "final_answer",
  "arguments": "image.png"
}

---
Task: "What is the result of the following operation: 5 + 3 + 1294.678?"

Action:
{
    "name": "python_interpreter",
    "arguments": {"code": "5 + 3 + 1294.678"}
}
Observation: 1302.678

Action:
{
  "name": "final_answer",
  "arguments": "1302.678"
}

---
Task: "Which city has the highest population , Guangzhou or Shanghai?"

Action:
{
    "name": "web_search",
    "arguments": "Population Guangzhou"
}
Observation: ['Guangzhou has a population of 15 million inhabitants as of 2021.']


Action:
{
    "name": "web_search",
    "arguments": "Population Shanghai"
}
Observation: '26 million (2019)'

Action:
{
  "name": "final_answer",
  "arguments": "Shanghai"
}

Above example were using notional tools that might not exist for you. You only have access to these tools:
- produce_and_execute_r: Produce an executable R script and write and execute the r script returning stdout
and stderr.
    Takes inputs: {'rscript': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The rscript to execute. This should be correct R.'}}
    Returns an output of type: string
- final_answer: Provides a final answer to the given problem.
    Takes inputs: {'answer': {'type': 'any', 'description': 'The final answer to the problem'}}
    Returns an output of type: any

Here are the rules you should always follow to solve your task:
1. ALWAYS provide a tool call, else you will fail.
2. Always use the right arguments for the tools. Never use variable names as the action arguments, use the value instead.
3. Call a tool only when needed: do not call the search agent if you do not need information, try to solve the task yourself. If no tool call is needed, use final_answer tool to return your answer.
4. Never re-do a tool call that you previously did with the exact same parameters.

Now Begin!

arguments.rscript:
# Load required packages
library(readr)
library(dplyr)
library(tidyr)
library(labelled)

# Function to map NVQ codes to 5-level NVQ scheme
# academic and vocational NVQ variables have values:
# -9 Refused, -8 Missing info, -1 Not applicable, 0 Entry Level, 1-5 NVQ levels, 95 other, 96 none
nvq_to_tier <- function(x){
  case_when(
    is.na(x) ~ NA_real_,
    x == -9 ~ -9,      # Refused
    x == -8 ~ -8,      # Missing info
    x == -1 ~ -1,      # Not applicable
    x == 0  ~ 2,       # Entry level -> tier 2
    x >= 1 & x <= 3 ~ 1,  # NVQ1-3 -> tier 1
    x >= 4 & x <= 5 ~ 0,  # NVQ4-5 -> tier 0
    x == 95 ~ 3,       # Other qualifications -> tier 3
    x == 96 ~ 4        # None of these -> tier 4
  )
}

# Load all files
wave_one <- read_delim("data/input/wave_one_lsype_young_person_2020.tab", delim = "\t", col_types = cols(.default = "guess"))
wave_four <- read_delim("data/input/wave_four_lsype_young_person_2020.tab", delim = "\t", col_types = cols(.default = "guess"))
ns8_main <- read_delim("data/input/ns8_2015_main_interview.tab", delim = "\t", col_types = cols(.default = "guess"))
ns8_derived <- read_delim("data/input/ns8_2015_derived.tab", delim = "\t", col_types = cols(.default = "guess"))
ns9_main <- read_delim("data/input/ns9_2022_main_interview.tab", delim = "\t", col_types = cols(.default = "guess"))
ns9_derived <- read_delim("data/input/ns9_2022_derived_variables.tab", delim = "\t", col_types = cols(.default = "guess"))

# Merge all datasets by NSID using full_join
merged <- wave_one %>%
  full_join(wave_four, by = "NSID") %>%
  full_join(ns8_main, by = "NSID") %>%
  full_join(ns8_derived, by = "NSID") %>%
  full_join(ns9_main, by = "NSID") %>%
  full_join(ns9_derived, by = "NSID")

# ---- educ25 (age 25, collapsed 5-level NVQ scheme) ----
# Map academic NVQ variable
acad_tier25 <- nvq_to_tier(merged$W8DHANVQH)

# Define mapping for each vocational tick box to NVQ tier
# Based on variable names; see metadata for mapping
voc_vars <- c("W8VCQU0A","W8VCQU0B","W8VCQU0C","W8VCQU0D","W8VCQU0E","W8VCQU0F","W8VCQU0G","W8VCQU0H","W8VCQU0I","W8VCQU0J","W8VCQU0K","W8VCQU0L","W8VCQU0M","W8VCQU0N","W8VCQU0O")
# Map each variable to a tier value (0-4) if Yes, otherwise NA
# We approximate tiers: Youth training, Key Skills, Basic skills, Entry level quals, Modern apprenticeship, RSA/OCR, City & Guilds, GNVQ/GSVQ, NVQ Level1-2, NVQ Level3-5, HNC/HND, ONC/OND, BTEC/BEC..., SCOTVEC, Other vocational
# Assign tiers:
#   Level 3-5 -> 0
#   Level 1-2, youth training, key skills, basic skills, modern apprenticeship, RSA, City & Guilds, GNVQ/GSVQ -> 1
#   Entry level quals -> 2
#   HNC/HND, ONC/OND, BTEC etc, SCOTVEC, Other vocational -> 0 (treated as NVQ4-5 equivalence)
#   None of the above handled separately

voc_tiers_map <- list(
  W8VCQU0A = 1, # Youth training certificate
  W8VCQU0B = 1, # Key Skills
  W8VCQU0C = 1, # Basic skills
  W8VCQU0D = 2, # Entry level qualifications (Wales)
  W8VCQU0E = 1, # Modern apprenticeship/trade apprenticeship
  W8VCQU0F = 1, # RSA/OCR/Clerical and commercial qualifications
  W8VCQU0G = 1, # City and Guilds Certificate
  W8VCQU0H = 1, # GNVQ/GSVQ
  W8VCQU0I = 1, # NVQ/SVQ - Level 1 - 2
  W8VCQU0J = 0, # NVQ/SVQ - Level 3 - 5
  W8VCQU0K = 0, # HNC/HND
  W8VCQU0L = 0, # ONC/OND
  W8VCQU0M = 0, # BTEC/BEC/TEC/EdExcel/LQL
  W8VCQU0N = 0, # SCOTVEC, SCOTEC or SCOTBEC
  W8VCQU0O = 0  # Other vocational, technical or professional
)

# Compute vocational tier per person: take highest tier (lowest numeric) among Yes entries
voc_tier25_vec <- apply(merged %>% select(all_of(voc_vars)), 1, function(row){
  # For each variable, check if Yes (1) and map tier
  tiers <- sapply(seq_along(row), function(i){
    val <- row[i]
    if(is.na(val)) return(NA_real_)
    if(val==1){
      voc_tiers_map[[voc_vars[i]]]
    } else if(val==0){
      NA_real_  # No qualification
    } else if(val==-9){
      -9
    } else if(val==-8){
      -8
    } else if(val==-1){
      -1
    } else {
      NA_real_
    }
  })
  # Filter valid tier numbers (0-4)
  valid <- tiers[tiers %in% 0:4]
  if(length(valid)>0){
    min(valid)  # best qualification
  } else {
    # No valid qualification; preserve most severe missing code if present
    if(any(tiers==-9)) return(-9)
    if(any(tiers==-8)) return(-8)
    if(any(tiers==-1)) return(-1)
    return(NA_real_)
  }
})

# Combine academic and vocational tiers: choose best (min numeric) among 0-4; if none, keep most severe missing code
educ25 <- mapply(function(a,v){
  # a and v may be NA or negative codes
  # Extract valid tiers
  vals <- c(a, v)
  valid <- vals[vals %in% 0:4]
  if(length(valid)>0){
    min(valid)
  } else {
    # No valid tier, keep most severe missing code
    if(any(vals==-9)) return(-9)
    if(any(vals==-8)) return(-8)
    if(any(vals==-1)) return(-1)
    return(NA_real_)
  }
}, acad_tier25, voc_tier25_vec)

# ---- educ32 (age 32, collapsed 5-level NVQ scheme) ----
# Map academic NVQ
acad_tier32 <- nvq_to_tier(merged$W9DANVQH)
# Map vocational NVQ
voc_tier32 <- nvq_to_tier(merged$W9DVNVQH)
# Combine: choose best tier among valid; if one missing and other valid use that; if both missing keep the one with higher severity
educ32 <- mapply(function(a,v){
  # Determine if values are valid tiers or negative
  a_valid <- !is.na(a) && a %in% 0:4
  v_valid <- !is.na(v) && v %in% 0:4
  if(a_valid && v_valid){
    min(a, v)
  } else if(a_valid){
    a
  } else if(v_valid){
    v
  } else {
    # both missing; keep most severe negative code
    if(!is.na(a) && a %in% c(-9,-8,-1,-3,-2)) return(a)
    if(!is.na(v) && v %in% c(-9,-8,-1,-3,-2)) return(v)
    return(NA_real_)
  }
}, acad_tier32, voc_tier32)

# ---- educadtl32 (detailed academic qualifications) ----
# Define substantive variable order
acad_vars <- paste0("W9ACQU0", LETTERS[1:19]) # A to S
# Function to compute code
educadtl32 <- apply(merged %>% select(all_of(acad_vars)), 1, function(row){
  # Map values
  subs_values <- row
  # Check for any -1
  if(any(subs_values==-1)) return(-1)
  # Check if all substantive are No (2) and no missing/-3/-9/-2
  if(all(subs_values==2) && all(!is.na(subs_values))){
    return(19) # None of these qualifications
  }
  # Check for missing or -3
  if(any(is.na(subs_values) | subs_values==-3)) return(-3)
  # Find first Yes (1)
  first_yes <- which(subs_values==1)[1]
  if(is.na(first_yes)){
    # No Yes but not all No? Might be mixture of No and missing? handled earlier
    return(-3)
  } else {
    return(first_yes) # integer code
  }
})
# Convert to factor with labels
acad_labels <- sapply(acad_vars, function(v){
  lbl <- attr(merged[[v]], "label")
  if(is.null(lbl)) lbl <- v
  sub(lbl, "^Academic qualifications gained - ", "")
})
acad_labels <- c(acad_labels, "None of these qualifications")
educadtl32_f <- factor(educadtl32, levels = c(1:19, -8,-9,-2,-1,-3), labels = c(acad_labels, "Don’t know", "Refused", "No answer", "Not applicable", "Not asked at fieldwork stage"))

# ---- educvdtl32 (detailed vocational qualifications) ----
# Define vocational variable order
voc_vars32 <- paste0("W9VCQU0", LETTERS[1:21]) # A to U
educvdtl32 <- apply(merged %>% select(all_of(voc_vars32)), 1, function(row){
  subs_values <- row
  # Non-substantive tick-boxes: -3 (Don’t know), -9 (Refused)
  if(any(subs_values==-1)) return(-1)
  if(all(subs_values==2) && all(!is.na(subs_values))){
    return(21) # None of these qualifications
  }
  if(any(is.na(subs_values) | subs_values==-3)) return(-3)
  first_yes <- which(subs_values==1)[1]
  if(is.na(first_yes)){
    return(-3)
  } else {
    return(first_yes)
  }
})
# Labels
voc_labels <- sapply(voc_vars32, function(v){
  lbl <- attr(merged[[v]], "label")
  if(is.null(lbl)) lbl <- v
  sub(lbl, "^Vocational qualifications gained - ", "")
})
voc_labels <- c(voc_labels, "None of these qualifications")
educvdtl32_f <- factor(educvdtl32, levels = c(1:21, -8,-9,-2,-1,-3), labels = c(voc_labels, "Don’t know", "Refused", "No answer", "Not applicable", "Not asked at fieldwork stage"))

# ---- Prepare final dataset ----
final_df <- merged %>% select(NSID) %>%
  mutate(
